      "id": "edgeport-echo",
      "title": "EdgePort + Echo",
      "narrative": {
        "what": "The EdgePort on its own, with Echo answering every request with 200 OK. No Dispatcher, Connect or database, so this is a ceiling for EdgePort alone, not for a full deployment.",
        "why": "The EdgePort is the only stateful piece of Routr. When it saturates, calls fail, no matter what runs behind it.",
        "how": "Smoke run: SIPp sends SIP MESSAGE requests over UDP, starting at 25 messages/s and adding 25 every minute, up to 200 messages/s. The first 30 s warm the EdgePort up and are not measured. The run stops at the first step where p99 MESSAGE-to-200 latency reaches 50 ms or failed requests reach 0.1%."
